{"id":"atlas-intro","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":3600,"height":160,"text":"**NOS Schedule / NOS · 1.43-B**\n\nExecution atlas / each schedule record owns a column. UI modes and inline callbacks are separate records, not extra FreeRTOS tasks. Core 'n/a' is unspecified, not proof of affinity. Cadences and screen-off conditions are copied from graph.json; dormant and C-only paths remain labelled.","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-00","type":"text","x":48,"y":356,"width":440,"height":992,"text":"**main task: UI loop, display ON**\n\nCore: 0\nPriority: 1 (8192 B stack)\n\nCadence: esp_timer paced ~60 Hz (fps_cap 60), 40 Hz authored clock; services every frame\n\nScreen off: n/a (display on)\n\n**Runs**\n• main / app_main UI loop\n• nos_frame_run / frame_run\n• Screen stack and transitions\n• Input recogniser and router\n• Scene record, damage diff and stripe raster\n• Frame pacer\n• Motion primitives\n• Services hub (svc_init / svc_tick)\n• Phone line pump and status reporter\n• Activity service (svc_activity)\n• System status service (svc_sys)\n• Alarms service\n• Timer service\n• Stopwatch service\n• Ringer and ring-screen manager\n• Workout session engine\n• GPS track recorder\n• Voice memo service\n• Background jobs monitor\n• Sports journal (sensor/event logger)\n• Preferences service (nos_prefs)\n• Diagnostics log\n• Live pref application\n• Power policy\n• Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|73 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"context-01","type":"text","x":544,"y":356,"width":440,"height":992,"text":"**main task: UI loop, AOD / SENSOR**\n\nCore: 0\nPriority: 1\n\nCadence: 20 ms loop (50 Hz); one frame and one services tick per second at 80 MHz\n\nScreen off: yes (dim or dark panel; sensors stay on)\n\n**Runs**\n• main / app_main UI loop\n• Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF\n• nos_frame_run / frame_run\n• Services hub (svc_init / svc_tick)\n• Wake service (config, learn, tick)\n• Power policy\n• Live pref application\n• Radio admission control\n• DFS / PM locks (80-240 MHz)\n• Diagnostics log\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|23 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-02","type":"text","x":1040,"y":356,"width":440,"height":992,"text":"**main task: UI loop, display OFF**\n\nCore: 0\nPriority: 1\n\nCadence: 20 ms loop (50 Hz); nos_bg_tick(1.0) once a second; no frames drawn\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• main / app_main UI loop\n• Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF\n• Services hub (svc_init / svc_tick)\n• Wake service (config, learn, tick)\n• Power policy\n• Live pref application\n• Radio admission control\n• USB command dispatcher (cmd_exec)\n• Heap diagnostics\n• Diagnostics log\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|16 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-03","type":"text","x":1536,"y":356,"width":440,"height":992,"text":"**svc_tick slow path (on UI task)**\n\nCore: 0\nPriority: 1\n\nCadence: act_tick, sys_tick, sports_tick 1 s; heart 60 s; weather check 10 s; nosact save 10 min when dirty\n\nScreen off: yes, at 1 Hz\n\n**Runs**\n• Services hub (svc_init / svc_tick)\n• Activity service (svc_activity)\n• System status service (svc_sys)\n• Sports journal (sensor/event logger)\n• Heart aggregation service\n• Weather service (source merge)\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|24 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-04","type":"text","x":2032,"y":356,"width":440,"height":992,"text":"**prefs_tick checkpoint (on UI task)**\n\nCore: 0\nPriority: 1\n\nCadence: 2 s after last edit, 10 s max age, retry 5 s; only when the persistence window is open\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• Preferences service (nos_prefs)\n• SD settings bank writer\n• hal_store (NVS + SD routing)\n• SD mount, lease and lock\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|26 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"context-19","type":"text","x":2528,"y":356,"width":440,"height":992,"text":"**nimble_host task**\n\nCore: 0\nPriority: configMAX_PRIORITIES-4\n\nCadence: event driven (GATT, scan, adv)\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• nimble_host task\n• BLE host, advertising, GATT and bonding\n• NUS transport and RX line ring\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|8 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"context-33","type":"text","x":3024,"y":356,"width":440,"height":992,"text":"**ble_control_tick callout**\n\nCore: 0\nPriority: NimBLE callout\n\nCadence: every 100 ms\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• ble_control_tick callout\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-05","type":"text","x":48,"y":1616,"width":440,"height":416,"text":"**flush task**\n\nCore: 1\nPriority: 4 (3 KB)\n\nCadence: per dirty stripe; queue depth 3\n\nScreen off: idle (nothing to draw)\n\n**Runs**\n• flush task\n• Display flush and QSPI panel driver\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-06","type":"text","x":544,"y":1616,"width":440,"height":416,"text":"**touch task**\n\nCore: 1\nPriority: 5\n\nCadence: 10 ms when ON, 40 ms otherwise\n\nScreen off: yes, still polled at 25 Hz\n\n**Runs**\n• touch task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-08","type":"text","x":1040,"y":1616,"width":440,"height":416,"text":"**dotbake task**\n\nCore: 1\nPriority: 1 (3 KB)\n\nCadence: boot only\n\nScreen off: n/a\n\n**Runs**\n• dotbake task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-07","type":"text","x":48,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**cmd task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 4 (6144 B)\n\nCadence: 50 ms; BLE XFR poll 50 ms\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• cmd task\n• SD transfer service (SDXFER v=2)\n• BLE XFR transfer service\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-09","type":"text","x":544,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**board-sense task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 2 (4 KB static)\n\nCadence: 20 ms cycle, 3 IMU reads (~150/s); battery sample 1 Hz; calendar day <= 1 Hz\n\nScreen off: yes, always\n\n**Runs**\n• board-sense task\n• Battery sampler and percent model\n• Pedometer calendar gate\n• Pedometer and walk detector\n• Double-knock detector\n• Wrist movement episode detector\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"context-10","type":"text","x":1040,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**board-fs task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 1 (4 KB)\n\nCadence: 100 ms loop; pedometer save 60 s (only when display not ON); CSV row 60 s; RTC maintain; SD retry\n\nScreen off: yes (pedometer save only runs when the display is not ON)\n\n**Runs**\n• board-fs task\n• RTC trust and write-back\n• SD mount, lease and lock\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|18 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"context-11","type":"text","x":1536,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**imu-sample task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 3\n\nCadence: 25/50/100 Hz while a manual recording runs\n\nScreen off: only if started manually\n\n**Runs**\n• imu-sample task\n• IMU recorder HAL (imu_hal.c)\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-12","type":"text","x":2032,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**imu-write task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 1 (6 KB)\n\nCadence: 20 ms while recording\n\nScreen off: only if started manually\n\n**Runs**\n• imu-write task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-13","type":"text","x":2528,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**sports_sd task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 1 (4 KB PSRAM)\n\nCadence: 1 s drain, 512-record batch; 20 ms when a query is pending\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• sports_sd task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-14","type":"text","x":3024,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**workout_sd task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 2 (6144 B)\n\nCadence: 500 ms; write if dirty and forced or 5 s since last try; checkpoint 30 s\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• workout_sd task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-15","type":"text","x":3520,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**track_save task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 1 (4 KB)\n\nCadence: one shot per track stop\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• track_save task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-16","type":"text","x":4016,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**memo_scan task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 1 (4 KB)\n\nCadence: one shot per Recorder scan\n\nScreen off: n/a\n\n**Runs**\n• memo_scan task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-17","type":"text","x":4512,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**asset-read task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 1\n\nCadence: on demand (orrery textures)\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• asset-read task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-18","type":"text","x":5008,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**wifi-settings task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 2 (6144 B)\n\nCadence: 100 ms; credential checkpoint 5 s after join\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• wifi-settings task\n• Wi-Fi station, setup AP, HTTP server, SNTP\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-20","type":"text","x":5504,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**weather task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 2 (8 KB)\n\nCadence: 1 s poll; fetch every 1800 s (60 s on failure, 10 s minimum gap); needs Wi-Fi and location\n\nScreen off: yes, while Wi-Fi is up\n\n**Runs**\n• weather task\n• Open-Meteo fetcher (weather_service.c)\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-21","type":"text","x":6000,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**voice task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 3 (10 KB PSRAM)\n\nCadence: C board only; not created on B\n\nScreen off: n/a\n\n**Runs**\n• voice task\n• Voice chat engine (C board only)\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-22","type":"text","x":6496,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**ota-upload task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 5 (4 KB)\n\nCadence: per HTTP /ota upload\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• ota-upload task\n• OTA updater\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"context-23","type":"text","x":6992,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**ota_url task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 5 (8 KB)\n\nCadence: per /ota_url request\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• ota_url task\n• OTA updater\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|5 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"context-24","type":"text","x":7488,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**ext task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 0 (4 KB PSRAM)\n\nCadence: wakes at most every 50 ms; BME280 2 s; APDS 400 ms; MAX30102 120 ms with lease, background 10 min (<=40 s); LTE 1.25 s\n\nScreen off: yes (modules idle out 8 s after the last getter)\n\n**Runs**\n• ext task (strap service)\n• Strap HAL contract and presence mask\n• MAX30102 HR driver (ext_hr)\n• GNSS driver (ext_gps)\n• LTE modem driver (ext_lte)\n• BME280 driver (ext_env)\n• APDS-9960 driver (ext_light)\n• Magnetometer driver (ext_mag)\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|9 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-25","type":"text","x":7984,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**exta audio task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 3 (4 KB)\n\nCadence: 4 ms I2S blocks while recording or playing\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• exta audio task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-26","type":"text","x":8480,"y":2300,"width":440,"height":632,"text":"**extf audio file task**\n\nCore: any\nPriority: 0 (4 KB)\n\nCadence: on demand\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• extf audio file task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-27","type":"text","x":48,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**pace esp_timer**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: esp_timer\n\nCadence: 1/fps_cap while the display is ON\n\nScreen off: stopped\n\n**Runs**\n• pace esp_timer (frame pacing)\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-28","type":"text","x":544,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**haptic esp_timer**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: esp_timer\n\nCadence: per vibration pattern segment\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• haptic esp_timer\n• Haptic driver (ext_haptic)\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-29","type":"text","x":1040,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**wifi_retry esp_timer**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: esp_timer\n\nCadence: 2 s doubling to 300 s while Wi-Fi is wanted and down\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• wifi_retry esp_timer\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-30","type":"text","x":1536,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**wifi_ap esp_timer**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: esp_timer\n\nCadence: 600 s one-shot per phone-setup session\n\nScreen off: yes\n\n**Runs**\n• wifi_ap esp_timer\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-31","type":"text","x":2032,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**airhop esp_timer**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: esp_timer\n\nCadence: never created: no caller of hal_wifi_air_start in the NOS build\n\nScreen off: n/a\n\n**Runs**\n• airhop esp_timer\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-32","type":"text","x":2528,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**imu-rate esp_timer**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: esp_timer\n\nCadence: 1e6/hz microseconds while a recording runs\n\nScreen off: only if started manually\n\n**Runs**\n• imu-rate esp_timer\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-34","type":"text","x":3024,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**BOOT button ISR (GPIO0)**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: ISR\n\nCadence: on edge, 25 ms debounce\n\nScreen off: yes; the only deep-sleep wake source\n\n**Runs**\n• BOOT button (GPIO0)\n• Input recogniser and router\n• Display power states ON/AOD/SENSOR/OFF\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|13 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-35","type":"text","x":3520,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**DMA-done ISR (QSPI)**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: ISR\n\nCadence: per DMA transfer\n\nScreen off: idle\n\n**Runs**\n• AMOLED panel 466x466 (CO5300 profile, QSPI)\n• flush task\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]\n⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps in scheduled components]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"context-36","type":"text","x":4016,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":440,"text":"**deep sleep (ext0)**\n\nCore: n/a\nPriority: n/a\n\nCadence: no execution; wake by GPIO0 low causes a cold boot\n\nScreen off: all sampling stops\n\n**Runs**\n• Deep sleep (ext0 GPIO0 wake)\n• Restart / Power off\n\n[[Engine and scheduling|Execution notes]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"rhythm-0","type":"text","x":48,"y":3908,"width":640,"height":1808,"text":"**Every frame**\n\n• main task: UI loop, display ON — esp_timer paced ~60 Hz (fps_cap 60), 40 Hz authored clock; services every frame\n\n• pace esp_timer — 1/fps_cap while the display is ON","color":"6"},
{"id":"rhythm-1","type":"text","x":744,"y":3908,"width":640,"height":1808,"text":"**Periodically**\n\n• main task: UI loop, AOD / SENSOR — 20 ms loop (50 Hz); one frame and one services tick per second at 80 MHz\n\n• main task: UI loop, display OFF — 20 ms loop (50 Hz); nos_bg_tick(1.0) once a second; no frames drawn\n\n• svc_tick slow path (on UI task) — act_tick, sys_tick, sports_tick 1 s; heart 60 s; weather check 10 s; nosact save 10 min when dirty\n\n• prefs_tick checkpoint (on UI task) — 2 s after last edit, 10 s max age, retry 5 s; only when the persistence window is open\n\n• touch task — 10 ms when ON, 40 ms otherwise\n\n• cmd task — 50 ms; BLE XFR poll 50 ms\n\n• board-sense task — 20 ms cycle, 3 IMU reads (~150/s); battery sample 1 Hz; calendar day <= 1 Hz\n\n• board-fs task — 100 ms loop; pedometer save 60 s (only when display not ON); CSV row 60 s; RTC maintain; SD retry\n\n• imu-sample task — 25/50/100 Hz while a manual recording runs\n\n• imu-write task — 20 ms while recording\n\n• sports_sd task — 1 s drain, 512-record batch; 20 ms when a query is pending\n\n• workout_sd task — 500 ms; write if dirty and forced or 5 s since last try; checkpoint 30 s\n\n• wifi-settings task — 100 ms; credential checkpoint 5 s after join\n\n• weather task — 1 s poll; fetch every 1800 s (60 s on failure, 10 s minimum gap); needs Wi-Fi and location\n\n• ext task — wakes at most every 50 ms; BME280 2 s; APDS 400 ms; MAX30102 120 ms with lease, background 10 min (<=40 s); LTE 1.25 s\n\n• exta audio task — 4 ms I2S blocks while recording or playing\n\n• wifi_retry esp_timer — 2 s doubling to 300 s while Wi-Fi is wanted and down\n\n• imu-rate esp_timer — 1e6/hz microseconds while a recording runs\n\n• ble_control_tick callout — every 100 ms","color":"6"},
{"id":"rhythm-2","type":"text","x":1440,"y":3908,"width":640,"height":1808,"text":"**Event-driven / one-shot**\n\n• flush task — per dirty stripe; queue depth 3\n\n• dotbake task — boot only\n\n• track_save task — one shot per track stop\n\n• memo_scan task — one shot per Recorder scan\n\n• asset-read task — on demand (orrery textures)\n\n• nimble_host task — event driven (GATT, scan, adv)\n\n• ota-upload task — per HTTP /ota upload\n\n• ota_url task — per /ota_url request\n\n• extf audio file task — on demand\n\n• haptic esp_timer — per vibration pattern segment\n\n• wifi_ap esp_timer — 600 s one-shot per phone-setup session\n\n• BOOT button ISR (GPIO0) — on edge, 25 ms debounce\n\n• DMA-done ISR (QSPI) — per DMA transfer","color":"6"},
{"id":"rhythm-3","type":"text","x":2136,"y":3908,"width":640,"height":1808,"text":"**While the screen is off**\n\n• main task: UI loop, AOD / SENSOR — yes (dim or dark panel; sensors stay on); 20 ms loop (50 Hz); one frame and one services tick per second at 80 MHz\n\n• main task: UI loop, display OFF — yes; 20 ms loop (50 Hz); nos_bg_tick(1.0) once a second; no frames drawn\n\n• svc_tick slow path (on UI task) — yes, at 1 Hz; act_tick, sys_tick, sports_tick 1 s; heart 60 s; weather check 10 s; nosact save 10 min when dirty\n\n• prefs_tick checkpoint (on UI task) — yes; 2 s after last edit, 10 s max age, retry 5 s; only when the persistence window is open\n\n• touch task — yes, still polled at 25 Hz; 10 ms when ON, 40 ms otherwise\n\n• cmd task — yes; 50 ms; BLE XFR poll 50 ms\n\n• board-sense task — yes, always; 20 ms cycle, 3 IMU reads (~150/s); battery sample 1 Hz; calendar day <= 1 Hz\n\n• board-fs task — yes (pedometer save only runs when the display is not ON); 100 ms loop; pedometer save 60 s (only when display not ON); CSV row 60 s; RTC maintain; SD retry\n\n• imu-sample task — only if started manually; 25/50/100 Hz while a manual recording runs\n\n• imu-write task — only if started manually; 20 ms while recording\n\n• sports_sd task — yes; 1 s drain, 512-record batch; 20 ms when a query is pending\n\n• workout_sd task — yes; 500 ms; write if dirty and forced or 5 s since last try; checkpoint 30 s\n\n• track_save task — yes; one shot per track stop\n\n• asset-read task — yes; on demand (orrery textures)\n\n• wifi-settings task — yes; 100 ms; credential checkpoint 5 s after join\n\n• nimble_host task — yes; event driven (GATT, scan, adv)\n\n• weather task — yes, while Wi-Fi is up; 1 s poll; fetch every 1800 s (60 s on failure, 10 s minimum gap); needs Wi-Fi and location\n\n• ota-upload task — yes; per HTTP /ota upload\n\n• ota_url task — yes; per /ota_url request\n\n• ext task — yes (modules idle out 8 s after the last getter); wakes at most every 50 ms; BME280 2 s; APDS 400 ms; MAX30102 120 ms with lease, background 10 min (<=40 s); LTE 1.25 s\n\n• exta audio task — yes; 4 ms I2S blocks while recording or playing\n\n• extf audio file task — yes; on demand\n\n• haptic esp_timer — yes; per vibration pattern segment\n\n• wifi_retry esp_timer — yes; 2 s doubling to 300 s while Wi-Fi is wanted and down\n\n• wifi_ap esp_timer — yes; 600 s one-shot per phone-setup session\n\n• imu-rate esp_timer — only if started manually; 1e6/hz microseconds while a recording runs\n\n• ble_control_tick callout — yes; every 100 ms\n\n• BOOT button ISR (GPIO0) — yes; the only deep-sleep wake source; on edge, 25 ms debounce","color":"6"},
{"id":"rhythm-4","type":"text","x":2832,"y":3908,"width":640,"height":1808,"text":"**Dormant / no execution**\n\n• voice task — C board only; not created on B\n\n• airhop esp_timer — never created: no caller of hal_wifi_air_start in the NOS build\n\n• deep sleep (ext0) — no execution; wake by GPIO0 low causes a cold boot","color":"6"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nos-prefs","type":"text","x":48,"y":5984,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**nos_prefs (RAM struct)**\n52 B in-RAM preference struct loaded at boot (SD banks first, NVS fallback). Defaults: aod 0, sensor_idle 1, fps_cap 60, face 0. Lost only if a save never lands.\n\nruns: RAM. Read by the engine every frame; written by apps then prefs_save().\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|15 gaps]]\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ram-svc-state","type":"text","x":584,"y":5984,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**RAM-only service state**\nStatic structs for timer, stopwatch, music, weather, heart, call and find state. All lost at reboot.\n\nruns: RAM.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ram-sms","type":"text","x":1120,"y":5984,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SMS inbox (RAM)**\nDriver inbox of 12 messages and a UI list of 16 plus unread count.\n\nruns: RAM. LTE strap only.\n\n`STUB`\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ram-touch-ring","type":"text","x":1656,"y":5984,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**Touch ring (16 entries)**\nRing handed from the touch task to the UI loop's touch_drain.\n\nruns: RAM.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ram-battery-ring","type":"text","x":48,"y":6336,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**BLE battery mV ring (unused)**\n1440 x mV ring that nothing fills.\n\nruns: RAM. Never written.\n\n`DEAD-CODE`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-stripe-buffers","type":"text","x":584,"y":6336,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**Stripe buffers (2 x 16 rows, DRAM)**\nInternal-DRAM stripe framebuffers that the renderer fills and the flush task consumes. Internal DRAM is nearly full.\n\nruns: DRAM.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-dma-buffers","type":"text","x":1120,"y":6336,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**DMA rotate buffers (2 x 8 rows)**\nDMA-capable buffers where the flush task writes the CCW-rotated stripe before QSPI transfer.\n\nruns: DRAM.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-gfx-rec","type":"text","x":1656,"y":6336,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**gfx_rec command record**\nUp to 320 recorded draw commands with bounding boxes and hashes used for damage diffing.\n\nruns: RAM.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ram-notifs","type":"text","x":48,"y":6900,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**Notification store (PSRAM)**\nsvc_big block of about 10 KB: 20 x svc_notif (236 B) plus phone flags. Cleared at boot, never persisted.\n\nruns: PSRAM. Written by svc_tick.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Services hub|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ram-nus-ring","type":"text","x":584,"y":6900,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NUS RX line ring (8 KB PSRAM)**\n[len:2][bytes] records written by the BLE host and drained by phone_tick; mutex guarded. A 2048 B assembler sits in front.\n\nruns: PSRAM. BLE writes, svc_tick reads.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 6 - Gadgetbridge inbound and outbound message audit and phone-link failure modes|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ram-hr-history","type":"text","x":1120,"y":6900,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**HR history ring (144 samples)**\nOne bpm per 10 minutes for 24 h in PSRAM, plus the svc_heart day min/max. Lost at reboot.\n\nruns: PSRAM. Written by the ext task.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ram-background","type":"text","x":1656,"y":6900,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**Background-job history (PSRAM)**\n13 x 2.8 KB job histories for the Jobs app. Cleared at reboot.\n\nruns: PSRAM. 1 Hz.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-layer-cache","type":"text","x":48,"y":7228,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**Layer cache rasters (3 x 434 KB)**\nThree retained 466x466 rasters in PSRAM.\n\nruns: PSRAM.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-dot-masks","type":"text","x":584,"y":7228,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**Dot masks (PSRAM)**\nAbout 550 KB of prebaked dot glyph masks.\n\nruns: PSRAM. Baked at boot.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-arc-masks","type":"text","x":1120,"y":7228,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**Arc text masks (PSRAM)**\nCurved-text masks capped at 448 KB.\n\nruns: PSRAM.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-native-arena","type":"text","x":1656,"y":7228,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**Native menu arena (PSRAM)**\nUnpack arena for the menu pixel blob.\n\nruns: PSRAM.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-blur-arenas","type":"text","x":48,"y":7556,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**Blur arenas (kblur / pblur / ui_blur)**\nkblur keeps 896 KiB of card slots. pblur (about 0.9 MB) and the ui_blur arena (up to 2.6 MB) are never allocated on device.\n\nruns: PSRAM. Only kblur allocates.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Followup 4 - Uncovered built files- blur pipeline, orrery shade, fonts|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-nosprefs","type":"text","x":48,"y":8096,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS nosprefs mirror**\nNVS blob 'nosprefs' in namespace wos: migration source and card-absent fallback for the preferences.\n\nruns: NVS. Written with the SD checkpoint; read at boot if SD is absent.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-prefs-overlay","type":"text","x":584,"y":8096,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS prefs_overlay**\nSmall NVS overlay of runtime-adjusted prefs kept alongside nosprefs.\n\nruns: NVS. Written by the prefs service.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-pedometer","type":"text","x":1120,"y":8096,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS pedometer (24 B)**\nToday's step record (version, day key, count) saved by board-fs every 60 s when dirty and only while the display is not ON; restored at boot.\n\nruns: NVS. 60 s, retry 5 s, plus shutdown flush.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-nosact","type":"text","x":1656,"y":8096,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS nosact (activity history)**\n92 B v2 blob holding day/week/hourly/active-minute history. Written by act_save on the UI task: dirty and 10 min, immediately at midnight.\n\nruns: NVS. In-frame commit.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Health and activity|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-nosalarm","type":"text","x":48,"y":8424,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS nosalarm (164 B)**\nEight 20 B alarm records plus count and version.\n\nruns: NVS. Written on each alarm edit; loaded at boot.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-wc","type":"text","x":584,"y":8424,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS nos_wc (world clock)**\n6 B blob of up to four favourite city indices. Written without readback.\n\nruns: NVS. On favourite change.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-sportsfood","type":"text","x":1120,"y":8424,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS sportsfood + sportsmarks**\nFood/water intake ledger (8200 B) and labelled quick-report markers (1032 B).\n\nruns: NVS. On intake or marker edits.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-sportstune","type":"text","x":1656,"y":8424,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS sportstune (gesture tuning)**\n20 B of walk and knock thresholds.\n\nruns: NVS. On Wrist tuning change.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-wake-cfg","type":"text","x":48,"y":8752,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS wake_cfg**\n48 B FNV-1a-checked raise-to-wake configuration written when the wake learn finishes.\n\nruns: NVS. On change.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-ext-cal","type":"text","x":584,"y":8752,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS ext_mag + ext_sea**\nCompass calibration (36 B) and barometer sea-level reference (4 B).\n\nruns: NVS. On a passing calibration or sea-level change.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-bat-cal","type":"text","x":1120,"y":8752,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS bat_cal**\nBattery calibration offset (4 B mV) written by the batcal command.\n\nruns: NVS. On batcal.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-weather-loc","type":"text","x":1656,"y":8752,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS weather_loc (44 B)**\nLatitude, longitude and city for the Wi-Fi forecast. The only writer is hal_weather_set_location, which nothing in the built NOS calls, so the key stays empty.\n\nruns: NVS. Read at weather task start.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-voice","type":"text","x":48,"y":9080,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS voice_chat + voice_hist (C only)**\nVoice config and a 3892 B checksummed chat history on the C board. Unused on B.\n\nruns: NVS. C board only.\n\n`STUB`\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-legacy","type":"text","x":584,"y":9080,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS orphaned legacy keys**\ncfg (40 B, read at boot), alarms, pip_memory, pip_care_a/b and lcd_gap. Left over from the old UI; nothing current writes them.\n\nruns: NVS. Inert.\n\n`DEAD-CODE`\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-nvs-phy","type":"text","x":1120,"y":9080,"width":480,"height":272,"text":"**NVS phy (RF calibration)**\nESP-IDF RF calibration namespace (cal_version, cal_mac, cal_data 1904 B). Owned by esp_phy, not NOS.\n\nruns: NVS. Written by the radio driver.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-settings","type":"text","x":48,"y":9620,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD settings banks (settings.0/1.bin)**\nAuthoritative copy of nosprefs on SD at /sdcard/watch/settings.0.bin and .1.bin: alternating checksummed 276 B banks with fsync and readback.\n\nruns: SD. Written by prefs_flush; loaded into RAM at boot.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Storage and persistence|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-wifi-cred","type":"text","x":584,"y":9620,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**Wi-Fi credentials (SD + NVS mirror)**\n98 B wifi_cred checkpointed to SD /watch/wifi/ banks with an NVS mirror. Credentials stay out of board records.\n\nruns: SD/NVS. Written 5 s after a successful join.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 3 - Complete NVS key and legacy-store ownership including core-apps legacy keys|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-sports","type":"text","x":1120,"y":9620,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD sports journal (.spt)**\n/sdcard/watch/sports/YYYYMMDD-events.spt and YYYYMMDD-HH-sensors.spt of 64 B checksummed records: activity, battery, power, wake, heart, raw IMU/ENV/GPS.\n\nruns: SD. Drained every 1 s by sports_sd.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|9 gaps]]\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"1"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-workouts","type":"text","x":1656,"y":9620,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD workouts banks**\n/sdcard/watch/workouts/workouts.0.bin and .1.bin: alternating 4304 B checksummed session and history banks. A RUNNING session restores as PAUSED.\n\nruns: SD. Checkpoint 30 s while running.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-imu","type":"text","x":48,"y":9972,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD IMU recordings**\n/sdcard/imu/NNNN.csv (4 MiB segments), .link files and intent.0/1.bin banks.\n\nruns: SD. While recording.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Sports and workouts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-tracks","type":"text","x":584,"y":9972,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD GPX tracks**\n/sdcard/watch/tracks/NNNN.gpx written once per track stop.\n\nruns: SD. On stop.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-memos","type":"text","x":1120,"y":9972,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD voice memos (WAV)**\n/sdcard/watch/memos/M_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_NNNN.wav, 16 kHz mono. .part files from interrupted recordings are never recovered.\n\nruns: SD. While recording.\n\n`PARTIAL`\n[[Utility apps|Open note]]","color":"3"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-diag","type":"text","x":1656,"y":9972,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD diagnostics ring (diag-NN.bin)**\n/sdcard/watch/diagnostics/diag-00..07.bin DLG1 ring files for power samples and state changes.\n\nruns: SD. 30 s samples.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-logs","type":"text","x":48,"y":10324,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD minute CSV logs**\n/sdcard/watch/logs/*.csv: one battery/IMU row per minute from board-fs.\n\nruns: SD. 60 s (retry 1 s if busy).\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-sd-sky","type":"text","x":584,"y":10324,"width":480,"height":296,"text":"**SD orrery textures (/sky)**\n/sdcard/sky/*.565 and *.rgba planet textures provisioned by hand; read-only for the watch.\n\nruns: SD. Read on demand.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Shell and faces|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-orrery-pack","type":"text","x":48,"y":10888,"width":480,"height":248,"text":"**Orrery static sky pack (flash)**\nCompiled-in belt, comets, spacecraft and event data (od_pack_jd 2461327.5, built 2026-10-14).\n\nruns: Flash. Read-only.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Shell and faces|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-flash-nf-fonts","type":"text","x":584,"y":10888,"width":480,"height":248,"text":"**nf_* font tables (flash .rodata)**\nAbout 281 KB of baked glyph tables.\n\nruns: Flash. Read-only.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 4 - Uncovered built files- blur pipeline, orrery shade, fonts|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-rtc-chip","type":"text","x":1120,"y":10888,"width":480,"height":248,"text":"**PCF85063 calendar registers**\nBCD UTC at registers 0x04-0x0A. Trusted at boot only if the OS and 12-hour bits are clear.\n\nruns: RTC chip. Written by rtc_maintain.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-rtc-diag","type":"text","x":1656,"y":10888,"width":480,"height":248,"text":"**Retained RTC RAM (diag, heap fails)**\nRTC RAM and RTC_NOINIT: fault slots, breadcrumbs and eight heap-failure slots that survive a warm reboot.\n\nruns: RTC RAM. Written by diag and heap hooks.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Settings and developer|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-coredump","type":"text","x":48,"y":11192,"width":480,"height":248,"text":"**Coredump partition**\nFlash partition written by the panic handler and read by host tools.\n\nruns: Flash. On crash.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]","color":"4"},
{"id":"storage-copy-store-ota-slots","type":"text","x":584,"y":11192,"width":480,"height":248,"text":"**OTA app slots (2 x 0x780000)**\nTwo OTA slots, the first at 0x20000. OTA writes the inactive one; NVS is preserved.\n\nruns: Flash. On OTA.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Connectivity and voice|Open note]]","color":"4"}
],
"edges":[]
}
